
==============================================================================
A. 171Yb+ detection rate: exact four-level Bloch steady state against (Gamma/18) s_o/[1 + (2/9) s_o] (Section 8.1)
==============================================================================
Gamma_S/2pi = 19.6230 MHz (partial), I_sat = 50.830 mW/cm^2, magic angle 54.7356 deg
s_o =  0.01: closed form 6.834530e+04 s^-1; max over B of R_o/closed = 0.99505 at B = 0.299 G (Zeeman 1.4 MHz/G x B = 0.42 MHz, pumping Gamma s_o/18 = 0.0109 MHz); at 1 G: 0.98391
s_o =  0.10: closed form 6.700811e+05 s^-1; max over B of R_o/closed = 0.99513 at B = 0.954 G (Zeeman 1.4 MHz/G x B = 1.34 MHz, pumping Gamma s_o/18 = 0.1090 MHz); at 1 G: 0.99481
s_o =  1.00: closed form 5.604315e+06 s^-1; max over B of R_o/closed = 0.99547 at B = 3.041 G (Zeeman 1.4 MHz/G x B = 4.26 MHz, pumping Gamma s_o/18 = 1.0902 MHz); at 1 G: 0.63594
s_o =  2.45: closed form 1.086592e+07 s^-1; max over B of R_o/closed = 0.99857 at B = 4.476 G (Zeeman 1.4 MHz/G x B = 6.27 MHz, pumping Gamma s_o/18 = 2.6709 MHz); at 1 G: 0.23987
-> the closed form is the CEILING of the exact rate to 0.15-0.5 %, not reproduced 'to nine digits' (M3a finding)

==============================================================================
B. Leakage prefactors from the angular algebra (Sections 8.1, 8.8): R_d, R_b at s_o = 0.1, B = 1 G, and Crain's s_o = 2.45
==============================================================================
s_o = 0.1, B = 1.0 G: R_d = 9.973 Hz (Noek 9.9208, Crain 14.8812); R_b = 0.6094 Hz (Noek (2/3) form 0.60634); R_b/R_d = 0.0611 (3/49 = 0.06122); slow/fast separation 3.22e+04
s_o = 2.45, B = 4.7 G: R_d = 248.9 Hz (Noek 243.0602, Crain 364.5904); R_b = 14.93 Hz (Noek (2/3) form 14.85539); R_b/R_d = 0.0600 (3/49 = 0.06122); slow/fast separation 2.88e+04
-> Noek's (2/3)(1/3) prefactor with s = s_o/3, i.e. R_d = (2/27)(Gamma/2) s_o (Gamma/2 Delta_HFP)^2; Crain's 1/3 is refuted

